CycloneDX schemas, vendored for offline validation
====================================================

These files are fetched, unmodified (except for the "$id" strip below), from:

  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CycloneDX/specification/master/schema/<name>

  - bom-1.6.schema.json
  - bom-1.7.schema.json
  - spdx.schema.json            (transitive $ref of both bom-1.6 and bom-1.7)
  - jsf-0.82.schema.json        (transitive $ref of both bom-1.6 and bom-1.7)
  - cryptography-defs.schema.json  (transitive $ref of bom-1.7 ONLY — new in 1.7)

Each file has had its top-level "$id" key REMOVED. The published schemas set
"$id" to an "http://cyclonedx.org/schema/..." URL; check-jsonschema resolves a
schema's relative $refs against its "$id" first, so with "$id" present it
would try to fetch spdx.schema.json / jsf-0.82.schema.json / etc. over the
network at validation time instead of using the local files passed via
--base-uri. That network fetch once hung the attestation job for hours —
hence stripping it.

The strip was done with:

    python3 -c 'import json,sys; p=sys.argv[1]; d=json.load(open(p)); \
      d.pop("$id",None); json.dump(d,open(p,"w"), indent=2)' <file>

Which bom-<version> schemas to vendor: scripts/enrich-sbom.py FLOORS every
SBOM's "specVersion" to "1.6" but does NOT cap it — so whatever CycloneDX
version Syft emits (>= 1.6) passes through unchanged. Today Syft emits 1.7, so
we vendor BOTH bom-1.6 and bom-1.7 (older cached SBOMs may still be 1.6).
spdx.schema.json and jsf-0.82.schema.json are spec-version-agnostic transitive
$refs shared by both; cryptography-defs.schema.json is referenced only by
bom-1.7. The full $ref closure resolves entirely to files in this directory
(verified: no external/network $refs remain).

If the SBOM's specVersion is ever bumped again (Syft upgrades its CycloneDX
output, e.g. to 1.8), the "Validate CycloneDX SBOM schema" step in
.github/workflows/build.yml will fail loudly (by design — no network
fallback). To fix: vendor the new bom-<version>.schema.json here using the
same fetch + strip steps above, then grep the new schema for '"$ref"' and
vendor any NEW transitive schema it pulls in (as bom-1.7 introduced
cryptography-defs) so the whole closure stays local.
